IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssa-common`
IMPORT `ssa-figures`
IMPORT `ssa-title-ii`
IMPORT `ssa-seat`

-- Social Security Act -- worked cases for the worker, the retiree and the working beneficiary (Title II).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand from
-- the deposited text (42 U.S.C. ch. 7 subch. II, OLRC release point Public Law 119-121) and the 2026 figures (90 FR 49047),
-- never copied from the encoding's output. All people are HYPOTHETICAL. Month numbers in the core rules are year x 12 +
-- month - 1; the seat questions take a year and a month.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 413: quarters of coverage in 2026, at $1,890 each, at most four.
-- $7,560 = 4 x $1,890: four. $5,000 / $1,890 = 2.6: two. $100,000: four, the cap.
#ASSERT `How many quarters of coverage do my earnings give me` 2026 7560 EQUALS `answered` 4
#ASSERT `How many quarters of coverage do my earnings give me` 2026 5000 EQUALS `answered` 2
#ASSERT `How many quarters of coverage do my earnings give me` 2026 100000 EQUALS `answered` 4
#ASSERT `How many quarters of coverage do my earnings give me` 2026 1889 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- 2025's amount is not deposited.
#ASSERT `How many quarters of coverage do my earnings give me` 2025 7560 EQUALS `not covered` `the figures the Act needs for that year are not deposited: only the 2026 Federal Register notices are`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 414(a): Ana, born 10 May 1964, reaches 62 in 2026. She turned 21 in 1985; the elapsed years are 1986-2025, 40 of them.
-- 40 quarters: fully insured (under both (1) and (2)). 39: not.
#ASSERT `Am I fully insured for retirement` (Date 10 5 1964) 40 0 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I fully insured for retirement` (Date 10 5 1964) 39 0 TRUE)
-- Two years in a period of disability are not elapsed years: 38 are needed, and 39 suffice.
#ASSERT `Am I fully insured for retirement` (Date 10 5 1964) 39 2 TRUE
-- A non-citizen without a work-authorised number does not meet s 414(c), whatever the quarters.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I fully insured for retirement` (Date 10 5 1964) 40 0 FALSE)
-- The elapsed years for Ana: 2026 - 1985 - 1 = 40.
#ASSERT `the elapsed years for fully insured status` (Date 10 5 1964) 2026 0 EQUALS 40
-- A worker who reached 21 before 1951 counts from 1951 (s 414(a)(1) "after 1950"): born 1920, 62 in 1982: 1951-1981, 31.
#ASSERT `the elapsed years for fully insured status` (Date 10 5 1920) 1982 0 EQUALS 31
-- Six quarters are always needed: elapsed years of 2 still need 6 (the "in no case ... unless ... at least 6" proviso).
#ASSERT NOT (`is a fully insured individual` 5 2 TRUE)
#ASSERT `is a fully insured individual` 6 2 TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 423(c)(1): Ben, born 15 March 1980, asks about June 2026 (age 46). Elapsed years for the fully-insured test as if 62 on
-- 1 June 2026: 2002-2025 = 24. With 80 quarters and 20 in the last 40: insured. With 19 in the last 40: not (he is past 31).
#ASSERT `Am I insured for disability benefits in the month` (Date 15 3 1980) 2026 6 80 20 80 12 0 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I insured for disability benefits in the month` (Date 15 3 1980) 2026 6 80 19 80 12 0 FALSE TRUE)
-- Blind: the 20-of-40 test does not apply; fully insured is enough.
#ASSERT `Am I insured for disability benefits in the month` (Date 15 3 1980) 2026 6 80 0 80 0 0 TRUE TRUE
-- Cleo, born 20 August 2000, asks about June 2026 (age 25). Quarters after the quarter she turned 21 (Q3 2021) up to and
-- including Q2 2026: Q4 2021, 4 in each of 2022-2025, Q1-Q2 2026 = 19, made even: 18; half is 9. Elapsed years 2022-2025 = 4,
-- so 6 quarters make her fully insured. With 12 quarters (10 since 21): insured; with 8 since 21: not; she is before the
-- quarter of age 31.
#ASSERT `Am I insured for disability benefits in the month` (Date 20 8 2000) 2026 6 12 12 10 8 0 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I insured for disability benefits in the month` (Date 20 8 2000) 2026 6 12 12 8 8 0 FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the quarters after age 21, made even` (Date 20 8 2000) (`the month number of` 2026 6) EQUALS 18
-- Dan, born 20 August 2004, asks about June 2026 (age 21): one quarter after Q3 2025 (Q4 2025) and Q1-Q2 2026 = 3, made
-- even 2, fewer than 12: 6 of the last 12 quarters are needed.
#ASSERT `Am I insured for disability benefits in the month` (Date 20 8 2004) 2026 6 6 6 3 6 0 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I insured for disability benefits in the month` (Date 20 8 2004) 2026 6 6 6 3 5 0 FALSE TRUE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 416(l): retirement age.
-- Born 10 May 1960: 62 in 2022, after 2021: 67, reached May 2027.
#ASSERT `When do I reach full retirement age` (Date 10 5 1960) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2027, `month` IS 5
-- Born 10 March 1955: 62 in 2017: 66 and 2 months (2/12 of the 12 months of 2017), reached May 2021.
#ASSERT `When do I reach full retirement age` (Date 10 3 1955) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2021, `month` IS 5
-- Born 1 January 1957: attains each age on 31 December (NOTES.md finding 1), so 62 on 31 December 2018: 66 and 4 months
-- (two-twelfths of the 24 months January 2017 to December 2018), from December 1956 + 66 years 4 months = April 2023.
#ASSERT `When do I reach full retirement age` (Date 1 1 1957) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2023, `month` IS 4
-- Born 15 June 1943: 62 in 2005: 66, June 2009. Born 15 December 1937: 62 in 1999: 65, December 2002.
#ASSERT `When do I reach full retirement age` (Date 15 6 1943) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2009, `month` IS 6
#ASSERT `When do I reach full retirement age` (Date 15 12 1937) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2002, `month` IS 12
-- Born 15 February 1940: 62 in 2002: 65 and 6 months (2/12 of the 36 months 2000-2002), August 2005.
#ASSERT `When do I reach full retirement age` (Date 15 2 1940) EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2005, `month` IS 8

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 415(a)(1): Ana's PIA with AIME of $3,000, first eligible 2026: 90% of $1,286 = $1,157.40, plus 32% of $1,714 = $548.48,
-- = $1,705.88, rounded down to $1,705.80.
#ASSERT `What is my primary insurance amount` (Date 10 5 1964) 3000 EQUALS `answered` 1705.8
-- AIME $10,000: $1,157.40 + 32% of $6,463 ($2,068.16) + 15% of $2,251 ($337.65) = $3,563.21, rounded down $3,563.20.
#ASSERT `What is my primary insurance amount` (Date 10 5 1964) 10000 EQUALS `answered` 3563.2
-- AIME $1,000: 90% = $900.
#ASSERT `What is my primary insurance amount` (Date 10 5 1964) 1000 EQUALS `answered` 900
-- Born 1963 (62 in 2025): the PIA has had the December 2025 increase and 2025's bend points are not deposited.
#ASSERT `What is my primary insurance amount` (Date 10 5 1963) 3000 EQUALS `not covered` `the PIA of a person first eligible before 2026 has been raised by cost-of-living increases that are not deposited`
-- Born 1966 (62 in 2028): no 2028 figures.
#ASSERT `What is my primary insurance amount` (Date 10 5 1966) 3000 EQUALS `not covered` `the figures the Act needs for that year are not deposited: only the 2026 Federal Register notices are`
-- Born 1915 (62 in 1977): before 1979.
#ASSERT `What is my primary insurance amount` (Date 10 5 1915) 3000 EQUALS `not covered` `the person was first eligible, or died, before 1979, so the old PIA rules in s 415(a)(4), (5) and (d) apply, which are not encoded`
-- s 415(b)(2)(A): Ana's 40 elapsed years less 5 = 35 computation years; total indexed earnings of $1,260,000 over 35 years
-- (420 months) = AIME $3,000.
#ASSERT `the number of benefit computation years for old-age or death` 40 EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `the average indexed monthly earnings` 1260000 35 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `the number of benefit computation years for old-age or death` 4 EQUALS 2
-- Disability at 46 with 24 elapsed years: less one-fifth (4) = 20.
#ASSERT `the number of benefit computation years for disability` 24 EQUALS 20

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 402(a), (j): when Ana's benefit can begin. She attains 62 in May 2026 but is not 62 throughout May (born on the 10th),
-- so June 2026 is the earliest month. Her retirement age month is May 2031.
-- Applying in March 2026: June 2026.
#ASSERT `From which month can my retirement benefit begin` (Date 10 5 1964) 2026 3 EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 6
-- Applying in September 2026: September 2026; no retroactive month, since it would be reduced (s 402(j)(4)(A)).
#ASSERT `From which month can my retirement benefit begin` (Date 10 5 1964) 2026 9 EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 9
-- Applying in August 2031, after retirement age: back to May 2031 (six months back would be February 2031, reduced).
#ASSERT `From which month can my retirement benefit begin` (Date 10 5 1964) 2031 8 EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2031, `month` IS 5
-- Applying in December 2031: six months back, June 2031 (s 402(j)(1)(B)).
#ASSERT `From which month can my retirement benefit begin` (Date 10 5 1964) 2031 12 EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2031, `month` IS 6
-- Born 2 May 1964: attains 62 on 1 May 2026, so 62 throughout May: applying in April 2026 gives May 2026.
#ASSERT `From which month can my retirement benefit begin` (Date 2 5 1964) 2026 4 EQUALS `Calendar month` WITH `year` IS 2026, `month` IS 5

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 402(q), (w), s 415(g): Ana's benefit on a PIA of $2,000.
-- From June 2026: 59 months before May 2031. 36 x 5/9% = 20%, 23 x 5/12% = 9.5833%: 29.5833% of $2,000 = $591.67, rounded
-- up to $591.70; $1,408.30, rounded down to $1,408.
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 10 5 1964) TRUE 2000 2026 6 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 1408
-- From May 2028, 36 months early: 20%, $400: $1,600.
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 10 5 1964) TRUE 2000 2028 5 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 1600
-- From May 2031, at retirement age: the PIA.
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 10 5 1964) TRUE 2000 2031 5 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 2000
-- From November 2032, 18 increment months at 2/3% (first eligible 2026, after 2004): 12%: $2,240.
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 10 5 1964) TRUE 2000 2032 11 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 2240
-- From May 2034, age 70: 36 increment months, 24%: $2,480. Waiting beyond 70 adds nothing: June 2035, still $2,480.
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 10 5 1964) TRUE 2000 2034 5 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 2480
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 10 5 1964) TRUE 2000 2035 6 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 2480
-- At retirement age, after starting in June 2026 and having 12 months fully withheld for work: the adjusted reduction period
-- is 47 months: 20% + 11 x 5/12% = 24.5833%, $491.67 rounded up $491.70: $1,508.30, $1,508 (s 402(q)(7)(A)).
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 10 5 1964) TRUE 2000 2026 6 12 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 1508
-- On her 2026 PIA of $1,705.80 from June 2026: 29.5833% = $504.63, rounded up $504.70: $1,201.10, $1,201.
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 10 5 1964) TRUE 1705.8 2026 6 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 1201
-- Not fully insured: no benefit. May 2026: not 62 throughout the month.
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 10 5 1964) FALSE 2000 2026 6 0 EQUALS `no benefit` "not fully insured (s 402(a)(1), s 414(a))"
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 10 5 1964) TRUE 2000 2026 5 0 EQUALS `no benefit` "not yet 62 throughout the month (s 402(a)(2), (B))"
-- s 402(w)(6)(C): Eve, born 15 February 1940, first eligible 2002: 1/4% plus 1/24% for each odd year 1987-2001 (8 of them)
-- = 14/24 of 1% a month. Retirement age August 2005; starting at 70, February 2010: 54 increment months, 31.5%: PIA $1,000
-- becomes $1,315.
#ASSERT `How much is my retirement benefit` (Date 15 2 1940) TRUE 1000 2010 2 0 EQUALS `a monthly benefit of` 1315
#ASSERT `the delayed retirement percentage per month` 1979 EQUALS 0.0025
#ASSERT `the delayed retirement percentage per month` 1978 EQUALS 0.01 DIVIDED BY 12

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 403(a)(1): the family maximum for Ana (62 in 2026).
-- PIA $2,000: 150% of $1,643 = $2,464.50, plus 272% of $357 = $971.04: $3,435.54, rounded down $3,435.50.
#ASSERT `What is my family maximum` (Date 10 5 1964) 2000 EQUALS `answered` 3435.5
-- PIA $3,500: $2,464.50 + 272% of $728 ($1,980.16) + 134% of $722 ($967.48) + 175% of $407 ($712.25) = $6,124.39: $6,124.30.
#ASSERT `What is my family maximum` (Date 10 5 1964) 3500 EQUALS `answered` 6124.3
-- PIA $1,000: 150%, $1,500.
#ASSERT `What is my family maximum` (Date 10 5 1964) 1000 EQUALS `answered` 1500

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 403(b), (f): the earnings test in 2026.
-- Under retirement age all year, earnings $34,480: half of ($34,480 - $24,480) = $5,000, against $1,500 x 12 = $18,000.
#ASSERT `How much of my benefits will be withheld for my earnings` 2026 `under retirement age for the whole year` 34480 1500 12 EQUALS `answered` 5000
-- Earnings $74,480: excess $25,000, but no more than the $18,000 of benefits that can be charged.
#ASSERT `How much of my benefits will be withheld for my earnings` 2026 `under retirement age for the whole year` 74480 1500 12 EQUALS `answered` 18000
-- Earnings $20,000: below $24,480, nothing.
#ASSERT `How much of my benefits will be withheld for my earnings` 2026 `under retirement age for the whole year` 20000 1500 12 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- The year retirement age is reached, earnings before that month $75,160: one-third of ($75,160 - $65,160) = $3,333.33,
-- reduced to $3,333; four months to charge at $1,000: $4,000, so $3,333.
#ASSERT `How much of my benefits will be withheld for my earnings` 2026 `the year retirement age is attained` 75160 1000 4 EQUALS `answered` 3333
-- After the year of retirement age: no deduction.
#ASSERT `How much of my benefits will be withheld for my earnings` 2026 `retirement age attained before the year began` 200000 1000 12 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- 2027: not deposited.
#ASSERT `How much of my benefits will be withheld for my earnings` 2027 `under retirement age for the whole year` 34480 1500 12 EQUALS `not covered` `the figures the Act needs for that year are not deposited: only the 2026 Federal Register notices are`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 403(h): the report of earnings for 2026.
#ASSERT `Must I report my earnings for the year` 2026 TRUE `under retirement age for the whole year` 30000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I report my earnings for the year` 2026 TRUE `under retirement age for the whole year` 24000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I report my earnings for the year` 2026 TRUE `the year retirement age is attained` 60000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I report my earnings for the year` 2026 TRUE `the year retirement age is attained` 70000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I report my earnings for the year` 2026 TRUE `retirement age attained before the year began` 200000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I report my earnings for the year` 2026 TRUE `under retirement age for the whole year` 30000 TRUE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I report my earnings for the year` 2026 FALSE `under retirement age for the whole year` 30000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- By the 15th day of the fourth month after 2026: 15 April 2027; with the most extension, four months: 15 August 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I report my earnings` 2026 0 EQUALS Date 15 4 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I report my earnings` 2026 4 EQUALS Date 15 8 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I report my earnings` 2026 6 EQUALS Date 15 8 2027
-- s 403(h)(2): additional deductions. First failure: the last month's benefit, $1,500, or the deduction if smaller ($800),
-- but not less than $10. Second: twice. Third: three times. Good cause or no deduction: none.
#ASSERT `How much more is deducted for not reporting my earnings` 1 1500 5000 FALSE EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `How much more is deducted for not reporting my earnings` 1 1500 800 FALSE EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `How much more is deducted for not reporting my earnings` 1 1500 5 FALSE EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How much more is deducted for not reporting my earnings` 2 1500 5000 FALSE EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `How much more is deducted for not reporting my earnings` 3 1500 5000 FALSE EQUALS 4500
#ASSERT `How much more is deducted for not reporting my earnings` 1 1500 5000 TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much more is deducted for not reporting my earnings` 1 1500 0 FALSE EQUALS 0

-- The regulative rule: 105 days from 31 December 2026 to 15 April 2027. A report on day 100 (10 April 2027) fulfils it.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 403(h)(1)(A) -- a working beneficiary must report the year's earnings to the Commissioner` 2026 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the individual` `report earnings for the taxable year to the Commissioner` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- With a two-month extension (to 15 June 2027, day 166), a report on day 150 fulfils it.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 403(h)(1)(A) -- a working beneficiary must report the year's earnings to the Commissioner` 2026 2) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the individual` `report earnings for the taxable year to the Commissioner` 150)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the individual, "s 403(h)(2): ..." (no report by day 105, 15 April 2027)
#TRACE (`s 403(h)(1)(A) -- a working beneficiary must report the year's earnings to the Commissioner` 2026 0) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 106)
